--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

The licence above applies to the original code and content authored by
Sensory App House Ltd. Bundled third-party components are NOT relicensed and
remain under their own licences:

  • liblouis, and its translation tables — LGPL 2.1+ / GPL — © liblouis contributors
  • MathCAT   — MIT — © Neil Soiffer / DAISY Consortium
  • Temml     — MIT — the maths renderer in web/vendor/
  • Inter     — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — © the Inter Project Authors;
                the licence text travels beside the files as web/fonts/Inter-OFL.txt
  • Nemeth and UEB test corpora in Translate/tools/corpus/ — extracted from
                MathCAT's own test suite (MIT); provenance in that folder's NOTICE.md

NOT INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY, and why:
  • APH Braille Shadows (the braille typeface) — APH agreed we may USE it; that
    is not a grant to redistribute it, and APH publish it with no licence
    statement at all. web/fonts/PROVENANCE.md records the whole position. The
    braille pane falls back to Apple Braille / Segoe UI Symbol / monospace
    without it.
  • Rule summaries of the Nemeth 1972 code and the ICEB UEB Guidelines for
    Technical Material, and the harvested APH / BANA / NFB / SQA / UEB Online /
    UKAAF benchmark corpora. Those are other people's documents; the tools that
    read them fetch them on demand and never redistribute them.

Each such component is used under, and continues to be governed by, its own licence.
